{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WtGAJ8KDFbs62r9rgJimM7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence 7Li NMR or capillary\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient of lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/335119086_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering (Journal Article)\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/22082614\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (Journal Article)\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21547860\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient of lithium in molten xLi 2O-(1 - X)B 2O 3 system using high-temperature PFG NMR\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/255483868_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_lithium_in_molten_xLi_2O-1_-_XB_2O_3_system_using_high-temperature_PFG_NMR\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and Inter-diffusion Coefficients of Liquid Lithium Isotopes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/233155126_Self-diffusion_and_Inter-diffusion_Coefficients_of_Liquid_Lithium_Isotopes\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"The dynamics of liquid 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate measured with implanted-ion $^8$Li $\\\\beta$-NMR\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.03684\"}]\n\nThe search turned up one direct NMR measurement of liquid lithium self-diffusion, a neutron study, and simulations. Most results are abstracts only, and I found no capillary-method measurement specific to liquid lithium.\n\n- **NMR (1968):** A Journal of Chemical Physics paper from 1968 measured 7Li self-diffusion in liquid lithium by NMR. Its spin-echo method determined the diffusion coefficient from how the spin-echo signal depends on the amplitude of a pulsed magnetic field gradient. At the melting point, the reported value is D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10^-5 cm²/s, with (T/D)(dD/dT) = 2.8 ± 0.3. The temperature dependence is fit with an activation model, D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10^-3 exp[-(2300 ± 300 cal)/RT] cm²/s.\n- **Capillary method:** A book chapter on lithium self-diffusion lists data from NMR spin echo field gradient, capillary reservoir technique and quasi-elastic neutron scanning. The abstract does not give the lithium capillary values, so I could not confirm them. A separate source notes that a recently developed capillary method was used for tracer self-diffusion in liquid Na and K, not lithium.\n- **Neutron scattering:** A study used quasielastic coherent neutron scattering on liquid lithium to examine the temperature dependence of self-diffusion and compared it with incoherent scattering data.\n- **Simulation:** A molecular dynamics study found that the liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient increases with temperature and decreases with pressure. It reports good agreement with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure.\n- **Data scarcity:** Authors attribute the scarcity of experimental data to the higher radiation risk of the radiotracer measurement method.\n\nFor primary values, the 1968 NMR paper is the main source. For capillary-specific lithium data, the chapter's full text or a targeted search would be needed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edaeb32-3a5c-4882-8fb5-40e8344c9a44","uuid":"d623786f-5d1e-4801-961d-fb643bee5b14","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:12:39.462Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence 7Li NMR or capillary","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YbSMGUe89eVMFW6LhBtx7B","content":[{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient of lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/335119086_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_lithium"},{"title":"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering (Journal Article)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/22082614"},{"title":"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS","url":"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M/abstract"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (Journal Article)","url":"https://www.osti.gov/etdeweb/biblio/21547860"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient of lithium in molten xLi 2O-(1 - X)B 2O 3 system using high-temperature PFG NMR","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/255483868_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_lithium_in_molten_xLi_2O-1_-_XB_2O_3_system_using_high-temperature_PFG_NMR"},{"title":"Self-diffusion and Inter-diffusion Coefficients of Liquid Lithium Isotopes","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/233155126_Self-diffusion_and_Inter-diffusion_Coefficients_of_Liquid_Lithium_Isotopes"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225135828_Self-diffusion_coefficient_study_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"The dynamics of liquid 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium acetate measured with implanted-ion $^8$Li $\\beta$-NMR","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.03684"}]},"The search turned up one direct NMR measurement of liquid lithium self-diffusion, a neutron study, and simulations. Most results are abstracts only, and I found no capillary-method measurement specific to liquid lithium.\n\n- **NMR (1968):** A Journal of Chemical Physics paper from 1968 measured 7Li self-diffusion in liquid lithium by NMR. Its spin-echo method determined the diffusion coefficient from how the spin-echo signal depends on the amplitude of a pulsed magnetic field gradient. At the melting point, the reported value is D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10^-5 cm²/s, with (T/D)(dD/dT) = 2.8 ± 0.3. The temperature dependence is fit with an activation model, D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10^-3 exp[-(2300 ± 300 cal)/RT] cm²/s.\n- **Capillary method:** A book chapter on lithium self-diffusion lists data from NMR spin echo field gradient, capillary reservoir technique and quasi-elastic neutron scanning. The abstract does not give the lithium capillary values, so I could not confirm them. A separate source notes that a recently developed capillary method was used for tracer self-diffusion in liquid Na and K, not lithium.\n- **Neutron scattering:** A study used quasielastic coherent neutron scattering on liquid lithium to examine the temperature dependence of self-diffusion and compared it with incoherent scattering data.\n- **Simulation:** A molecular dynamics study found that the liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient increases with temperature and decreases with pressure. It reports good agreement with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure.\n- **Data scarcity:** Authors attribute the scarcity of experimental data to the higher radiation risk of the radiotracer measurement method.\n\nFor primary values, the 1968 NMR paper is the main source. For capillary-specific lithium data, the chapter's full text or a targeted search would be needed."],"durationSeconds":9.126752814000007,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WtGAJ8KDFbs62r9rgJimM7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
