{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111NejZvdTvzYoWALg7LbJB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium density temperature correlation kg/m3 ρ = 562 - 0.1 T\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Compilation of thermophysical properties of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Literature review of lead-lithium thermophysical properties - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0920379618307361?via=ihub%3D\"},{\"title\":\"Summary of Physical Properties for Lithium, Pb-17Li, and (LiF)n•BeF2 Coolants\",\"url\":\"https://bpb-us-w2.wpmucdn.com/research.seas.ucla.edu/dist/d/39/files/2019/08/1zinkle0798.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LITHIUM (Li)\",\"url\":\"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html\"},{\"title\":\"Pressure induced Structure Change and Anomalies in Thermodynamic Quantities and Transport Properties in Liquid Lithium Hydride\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.15532\"},{\"title\":\"Quasi-solid state microscopic dynamics in equilibrium classical liquids: Self-consisnent relaxation theory\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.06241\"},{\"title\":\"The INL is a U.S. Department of Energy National Laboratory\",\"url\":\"https://inldigitallibrary.inl.gov/sites/sti/sti/5698704.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Usage of Liquid Metals in the Positron Production System of Linear Collider\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1511.03571\"},{\"title\":\"Densities and apparent molar volumes of aqueous LiI solutions at temperatures from (296 to 600) K and at pressures up to 30 MPa - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0021961404001144\"}]\n\nThe search turned up one direct match for the correlation. A 1968 NASA compilation of thermophysical properties of liquid lithium lists lithium density as ρ = 562 − 0.100T, with T in kelvin and density in kg/m³. The correlation appears as \"Lithium density (p = 562 - 0.100 TI.\" The text is OCR-garbled, but the coefficients are legible.\n\nThe same document says the resulting correlation exhibits a minimum at about 1600 K. A straight line like 562 − 0.1T has no minimum, so that statement probably refers to a different fit in the report. I'd treat it as unresolved rather than as a property of this correlation.\n\nAs a spot check, the formula gives about 510 kg/m³ at 523 K (250 °C). A separate property table lists 510.0 kg/m³ at 250 °C, which agrees. The table's density falls to 495 kg/m³ at 400 °C, and the formula gives about 495 kg/m³ at 673 K, so the two also agree there.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edaeb32-3a5c-4882-8fb5-40e8344c9a44","uuid":"727afc47-24e4-4951-8382-d1a06238474e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:12:52.396Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium density temperature correlation kg/m3 ρ = 562 - 0.1 T","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BV14g57WPffnyJkVfC12nz","content":[{"title":"Compilation of thermophysical properties of liquid lithium","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf"},{"title":"Literature review of lead-lithium thermophysical properties - ScienceDirect","url":"https://sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0920379618307361?via=ihub%3D"},{"title":"Summary of Physical Properties for Lithium, Pb-17Li, and (LiF)n•BeF2 Coolants","url":"https://bpb-us-w2.wpmucdn.com/research.seas.ucla.edu/dist/d/39/files/2019/08/1zinkle0798.pdf"},{"title":"LITHIUM (Li)","url":"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html"},{"title":"Pressure induced Structure Change and Anomalies in Thermodynamic Quantities and Transport Properties in Liquid Lithium Hydride","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.15532"},{"title":"Quasi-solid state microscopic dynamics in equilibrium classical liquids: Self-consisnent relaxation theory","url":"https://ar